            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Craig Hennager"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Need to mention in the recipe whether or not to cool The Filling before putting it in the pie most people know you should but you should really write it so people that don't cook and know that little tip don't mess up their Pie by dumping that hot feeling into their pie cause the recipe doesn't really state what to do after you take it off the heat or how long it should be cool before putting it in your pie shell",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-14T17:43:11.792Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This pie was different! I've never had anything quite like it--and you must be a true raisin lover to enjoy it! I read through the reviews prior to making it, and I'm glad I did. The pie would have turned out sickeningly sweet had I followed the recipe as written. Since I made a smaller pie to begin with, I had already reduced the ingredients to about 3/4 the original amounts. So for 1 1/2 cups of raisins, I used 3 tablespoons of sugar--and that was plenty! I couldn't imagine adding in the full amount; it would've been overpowering. I also added some salt and cinnamon to the filling; and those were both welcome additions. My husband really loves raisins, so he enjoyed this pie a lot. I would've rated it higher, but the sugar amount listed in this recipe is far too much. Adjust that to your owns tastes, though, and you'll have a pie unlike any other! Thank you so much for sharing your recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-28T17:53:59.941Z"
          },
